diff --git a/docs/webhooks.md b/docs/webhooks.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bc7d7fe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/webhooks.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Board webhooks
+
+Manage webhooks from a board's existing Webhooks settings. Only active webhooks
+subscribed to an event's action receive it; webhooks on other boards do not.
+Delivery records are created in the event transaction, and delivery jobs are
+enqueued after commit.
+
+## Requests and logs
+
+Fizzy sends a JSON POST containing the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`,
+`eventable`, `board`, and `creator`. URLs in the payload include the account
+prefix. The request has these headers:
+
+- `Content-Type: application/json`
+- `X-Webhook-Id`: the delivery ID, stable across duplicate job executions
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: when the request was prepared, in ISO 8601 format
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hexadecimal HMAC-SHA256 of the exact request body,
+  using the webhook's signing secret
+
+Verify the signature with a constant-time comparison before processing the
+request. A 2xx response is success. Other HTTP statuses and transport errors
+count as failures. Redirects are not followed; private network destinations are
+blocked, and DNS results are pinned to the connection. Connection, read, and
+write timeouts are ten seconds each.
+
+The board's delivery log shows the state and HTTP status or error. The delivery
+API exposes sanitized request headers and a response summary, without the
+signature or request body. Log entries older than seven days are deleted by the
+existing cleanup task, which runs every fifteen minutes.
+
+## Delivery semantics
+
+Each webhook/event pair has a unique delivery record. A job atomically claims
+that record before sending, and only a pending record can be claimed. Neither
+failed deliveries nor ambiguous in-progress deliveries are resent. HTTP retries
+are also disabled.
+
+This provides **at most one POST attempt**, including when jobs are duplicated.
+True exactly-once receipt or processing cannot be guaranteed by a sender over
+HTTP: a worker can stop before sending, or a receiver can process a request and
+lose its response. In-progress records after a worker crash have an unknown
+outcome and are deliberately not retried. Receivers should persist and deduplicate
+the event ID (scoped to the webhook) alongside their processing if exactly-once
+side effects are required. The seven-day log is not a permanent deduplication
+ledger; retained historical events should not be manually redispatched after
+logs have expired.
+
+## Automatic deactivation
+
+A webhook is deactivated after at least ten consecutive failures whose first
+failure was at least one hour ago. Ten rapid failures alone do not deactivate
+it, nor do fewer than ten failures spread over an hour. A successful delivery
+resets both the count and the first-failure time.
+
+Manual reactivation also resets the streak. Queued deliveries that have not
+started when a webhook is deactivated are logged as `webhook_inactive` without
+making a POST. Already-started requests cannot be recalled.
diff --git a/test/models/webhook/delinquency_tracker_test.rb b/test/models/webhook/delinquency_tracker_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8bd1791
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/models/webhook/delinquency_tracker_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class Webhook::DelinquencyTrackerTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  setup do
+    @webhook = webhooks(:active)
+    @tracker = @webhook.create_delinquency_tracker!
+    @failure = webhook_deliveries(:unsuccessfully_completed)
+    @success = webhook_deliveries(:successfully_completed)
+  end
+
+  test "ten consecutive failures spanning an hour deactivate a webhook" do
+    freeze_time do
+      9.times { @tracker.record(@failure) }
+      assert @webhook.reload.active?
+      travel 1.hour
+      @tracker.record(@failure)
+      assert_not @webhook.reload.active?
+      assert_equal 10, @tracker.reload.consecutive_failures_count
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "neither ten failures within an hour nor nine failures over an hour deactivate" do
+    freeze_time do
+      10.times { @tracker.record(@failure) }
+      assert @webhook.reload.active?
+      @tracker.reset
+      @tracker.record(@failure)
+      travel 2.hours
+      8.times { @tracker.record(@failure) }
+      assert @webhook.reload.active?
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "success resets the failure count and start time" do
+    9.times { @tracker.record(@failure) }
+    @tracker.record(@success)
+    assert_equal 0, @tracker.reload.consecutive_failures_count
+    assert_nil @tracker.first_failure_at
+
+    freeze_time do
+      @tracker.record(@failure)
+      assert_equal 1, @tracker.reload.consecutive_failures_count
+      assert_equal Time.current, @tracker.first_failure_at
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "manual reactivation resets delinquency" do
+    @tracker.update!(consecutive_failures_count: 10, first_failure_at: 2.hours.ago)
+    @webhook.deactivate
+    @webhook.activate
+    assert @webhook.reload.active?
+    assert_equal 0, @tracker.reload.consecutive_failures_count
+    assert_nil @tracker.first_failure_at
+  end
+end
